# Test: the plugin registry refuses a registration made after start-up
# Exercises: main (cmd/ze/main.go) -> registry.Seal before dispatchMain
#            -> ze start -> the in-process test plugin lateregister
#            (internal/test/plugins/lateregister) -> OnAllPluginsReady -> probe
#            -> registry.Register -> refuseSealedLocked
#            (internal/component/plugin/registry/seal.go); then the same plugin
#            dispatches `show plugin list` and `request shutdown` to the daemon.
# QUESTION:  does the REAL binary seal its registry before it runs anything, so
#            a registering call from run-time code is refused while init()
#            registration still works? A unit test cannot decide it: no test
#            calls main, so only the built ze shows whether main seals.
# VALIDATES: spec-inventory-fast-registry-checks AC-6: the late Register call
#            meets ErrRegistrySealed, the daemon keeps answering commands, its
#            `show plugin list` lists lateregister under its init() name and not
#            the late name, and the daemon stops cleanly (exit 0).
# PREVENTS:  a registry that accepts a registration after start-up, which the
#            declared registration walk cannot see, so the binary would carry
#            a plugin the source does not declare.

option=timeout:value=30s

tmpfs=ze-sealed.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	internal lateregister {
		use lateregister
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze start ze-sealed.conf:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=lateregister: late registration refused: registry: sealed after start-up: plugin "lateregister-after-start"
expect=stderr:contains=lateregister: show plugin list lists lateregister and not lateregister-after-start
reject=stderr:contains=lateregister: FAIL
